:: WitchEctoplasmQuest [nobr] {"position":"1450,275","size":"100,100"}
/* Placeholder for the witch's ectoplasm-unlock quest. The real beats
   land later; for now the passage exists to keep the unlock loop
   closed -- one click here flips ectoplasmQuestStage to COMPLETED,
   which is the single gate the rest of the codebase reads
   (setup.Witch.ectoplasmUnlocked) for the rogue/random hunt card,
   the ectoplasm sidebar line, the WitchSummary payout, and the
   meta-shop link. */
<<if setup.Witch.ectoplasmQuestComplete()>>
	@@.notmc-speech; That ledger's open between us now. Don't waste the line.@@<br>
	<br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Back|WitchInside]]@@
<<else>>
	@@.location; Khadija's back room@@<br>
	@@.notmc-speech; Sit. This part isn't for the contract board.@@<br>
	@@.mc-speech; What is it?@@<br>
	@@.notmc-speech; A favor. Quiet kind. When you've done it, we'll have a different way of doing business -- you'll see what I mean.@@<br>
	@@.mc-thoughts; [Placeholder quest. The witch hands you a one-step errand to stand in for the real arc.]@@<br>
	<br>
	@@.usebtn;<<link "Handle it.">>
		<<run setup.Witch.completeEctoplasmQuest()>>
		<<goto "WitchEctoplasmQuestDone">>
	<</link>>@@<br>
	<br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Not now|WitchInside]]@@
<</if>>

:: WitchEctoplasmQuestDone [nobr] {"position":"1550,275","size":"100,100"}
/* Single-shot turn-in screen for the placeholder quest. By the time
   the player lands here the unlock has already flipped (setup.Witch
   .completeEctoplasmQuest fires on the click in WitchEctoplasmQuest),
   so the witch acknowledges and the ectoplasm UI starts surfacing
   from here on. */
@@.notmc-speech; Done. Cleaner than I thought.@@<br>
@@.mc-speech; And the other ledger?@@<br>
@@.notmc-speech; Houses bleed something the rest of the town doesn't see. You'll start spotting it. Bring me jars -- I'll trade.@@<br>
<br>
@@.mc-action; The ectoplasm economy is now open. Rogue addresses appear on the map; Khadija's ectoplasm wares are stocked.@@<br>
<br>
@@.backbtn; [[Back|WitchInside]]@@
